exports[`golden — SKILL.md > default schema 1`] = `
"# Clean Professional — Design System Skill

This file tells an AI agent how to build UI that conforms to this design system.
The normative source of truth is \`design-spec.schema.json\`; \`DESIGN.md\` carries the human rationale.

## Golden rule

Always reference design tokens. Never hard-code raw values (hex, px, \`Color(0xFF…)\`).
Raw values are *drift* and are auto-rewritten to the nearest token by \`design-spec fix\` and the CI Drift-Janitor.

## Getting context efficiently

Run \`design-spec serve\` to expose this schema over MCP. Request only the slice you need:
- \`get_component_tokens("Button")\` — tokens for one component.
- \`get_layout_system()\` — grid, spacing, container, breakpoints.
- \`get_semantic_colors()\` — semantic color roles (not the raw palette).

## Frameworks

### React + Tailwind

- Reference tokens via Tailwind utilities, never inline hex. e.g. \`className="text-primary rounded-md"\`.
- Token names map 1:1 to \`tailwind.config.js\` theme keys generated from the schema.
- Never write \`text-[#...]\` arbitrary values — that is drift and will be auto-fixed.

## Components

#### Button
A clickable action trigger. Primary drives the single most important action per view.
- Anatomy: root › label › icon › spinner
- Variants: primary, secondary · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: default, hover, focus, disabled, loading
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(primary|secondary)
  - \`size\`: enum(sm|md|lg)
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`loading\`: boolean
  - \`children\`: slot — Button label content.

#### Input
A single-line text field with label, helper text, and error states.
- Anatomy: root › label › field › helper
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: default, focus, disabled, error
- Props:
  - \`label\`: string
  - \`placeholder\`: string
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`error\`: string — Error message; switches the field to its error state.
"
`;

exports[`golden — SKILL.md > renders per-component responsive snippets 1`] = `
"# Responsive Fixture — Design System Skill

This file tells an AI agent how to build UI that conforms to this design system.
The normative source of truth is \`design-spec.schema.json\`; \`DESIGN.md\` carries the human rationale.

## Golden rule

Always reference design tokens. Never hard-code raw values (hex, px, \`Color(0xFF…)\`).
Raw values are *drift* and are auto-rewritten to the nearest token by \`design-spec fix\` and the CI Drift-Janitor.

## Getting context efficiently

Run \`design-spec serve\` to expose this schema over MCP. Request only the slice you need:
- \`get_component_tokens("Button")\` — tokens for one component.
- \`get_layout_system()\` — grid, spacing, container, breakpoints.
- \`get_semantic_colors()\` — semantic color roles (not the raw palette).

## Frameworks

### React + Tailwind

- Reference tokens via Tailwind utilities, never inline hex. e.g. \`className="text-primary rounded-md"\`.
- Token names map 1:1 to \`tailwind.config.js\` theme keys generated from the schema.
- Never write \`text-[#...]\` arbitrary values — that is drift and will be auto-fixed.

## Components

#### Button
A clickable action trigger. Primary drives the single most important action per view.
- Anatomy: root › label › icon › spinner
- Variants: primary, secondary · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: default, hover, focus, disabled, loading
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(primary|secondary)
  - \`size\`: enum(sm|md|lg)
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`loading\`: boolean
  - \`children\`: slot — Button label content.
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (tablet): paddingX: {spacing.lg} — comfortable padding
  - ≥1024px (desktop): paddingX: {spacing.xl}; paddingY: {spacing.md} — wider hit target

#### Input
A single-line text field with label, helper text, and error states.
- Anatomy: root › label › field › helper
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: default, focus, disabled, error
- Props:
  - \`label\`: string
  - \`placeholder\`: string
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`error\`: string — Error message; switches the field to its error state.
"
